Standalone canvas prototype
---------------------------

The new canvas uses Syspresent JavaScript (Apache-2.0), OpenSysML Go/WASM
(Apache-2.0), the Go browser runtime (BSD-3-Clause), fflate 0.8.2 (MIT),
and elkjs 0.12.0 (EPL-2.0 option of EPL-2.0 OR GPL-3.0-or-later).
ELK supplies disposable layout geometry in its own browser worker. Native
OpenSysML remains the semantic authority. This canvas does not bundle the
VS Code renderer or libavoid. The static build includes LICENSE,
engine/OPENSYSML-LICENSE, engine/GO-LICENSE, notices/fflate-LICENSE,
notices/elkjs-LICENSE, the unmodified ELK API and worker source, package
metadata and lockfile. ELK source: https://github.com/kieler/elkjs/tree/v0.12.0
Published source package: https://registry.npmjs.org/elkjs/-/elkjs-0.12.0.tgz. engine/provenance.json records the exact source,
carried patch and binary hashes. build-inputs.json records browser inputs.
The reproducible engine source patch and its original base are retained in
scripts/wasm-prototype; no upstream dependency PR is needed to rebuild it.

Previous viewer inventory
-------------------------

Third-party materials used by the browser build
=============================================

Syspresent's browser build reuses selected native OpenSysML browser modules.
Original Syspresent code is covered by the repository Apache-2.0 LICENSE.

The inspected build/viewer/build-inputs.json includes:

* OpenSysML browser source — Apache License 2.0. Source repository:
  https://github.com/DavidIngraham/OpenSysML
* elkjs 0.12.0 — package metadata declares EPL-2.0 OR GPL-3.0-or-later;
  its distributed LICENSE.md contains Eclipse Public License 2.0.
  Source repository: https://github.com/kieler/elkjs
* libavoid-js 0.4.5 — package metadata declares LGPL-2.1-or-later;
  its distributed LICENSE contains GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1.
  Source repository: https://github.com/Aksem/libavoid-js

The libavoid JavaScript glue is bundled. Its separate WASM loading path is
not evidence that a WASM resource was included in the inspected browser output.
The generated package archives exclude WASM binaries. This viewer does not call
loadAvoid; these notices do not introduce a runtime WASM distribution.

Generate distribution-specific notices after bundling and before hashing the
browser snapshot:

  OPENSYSML_SOURCE=/path/to/pinned/checkout node scripts/third_party_notices.mjs build/browser

The build can also import generateThirdPartyNotices(outputDir). It reads the
actual output build-inputs.json, verifies package versions against the source
package-lock.json, and writes output/notices/: full supplied license texts and
notices, exact bundled OpenSysML/dependency input files, installed dependency
archives excluding WASM and including available source maps, lockfile and a hash/provenance manifest.
Generated third-party source remains in build output, not tracked Syspresent
source. Include the entire notices directory in the distributable snapshot and
its hash manifest.

Limits requiring release review
-------------------------------

An installed npm archive is not automatically complete corresponding source.
Only libavoid-js JavaScript glue is bundled here; no WASM binary is distributed.
Its distribution may omit underlying C++ and build inputs;
ELK's generated distribution may also need its upstream preferred sources.
Repository and exact distribution links are retained, but this generator does
not certify completeness, source-offer sufficiency or replacement/relinking
arrangements. Preserve package-internal copyright/license headers, and resolve
the applicable source-availability obligations before distribution. This notice
is an inventory and provenance mechanism, not a legal compliance conclusion.

The source Git revision, dirty-checkout status, lockfile digest and exact bundled
input hashes are recorded per build. Build-only tools such as esbuild are not
listed as browser-bundled dependencies merely because they were used to build.
